The SIL OFL requires the font name and licence to accompany the font
when someone redistributes it. This repository does not redistribute
the OFL fonts. It downloads them at render time from their pinned
upstream sources. The GUST licence of the bundled Pagella fonts is
satisfied by the licence file shipped alongside them.

## Build-time tool dependencies (installed, not bundled)

| Tool | Licence | Source | Used by |
|---|---|---|---|
| pikepdf | BSD-3-Clause (https://opensource.org/license/bsd-3-clause) | PyPI `pikepdf` | `tools/attach-provenance.py` (embeds the source and manifest with the AFRelationship and MIME keys PDF/A-4f requires) |

pikepdf is a Python dependency of the Typst provenance gate only. It
is not imported by the LaTeX path, which embeds provenance during the
LaTeX run. `render.sh` resolves it from an explicit `PIKEPDF_PY`, a
`python3` with pikepdf importable, or the pdf2quarto virtualenv.

